{"title":"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Alternative_finish\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Alternative finish</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Easier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Easier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Even_Easier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Even Easier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OnTheSpotSTEM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OnTheSpotSTEM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Debra flips a fair coin repeatedly, keeping track of how many heads and how many tails she has seen in total, until she gets either two heads in a row or two tails in a row, at which point she stops flipping. What is the probability that she gets two heads in a row but she sees a second tail before she sees a second head？\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/9/dd90e5c1235f511e86448daad998b725b9a91845.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{1}{36} \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } \\frac{1}{24} \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } \\frac{1}{18} \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } \\frac{1}{12} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } \\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"408\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first want to find out which sequences of coin flips satisfy the given condition. For Debra to see the second tail before the second head, her first flip can't be heads, as that would mean she would either end with double tails before seeing the second head, or would see two heads before she sees two tails. Therefore, her first flip must be tails. The shortest sequence of flips by which she can get two heads in a row and see the second tail before she sees the second head is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/4/534df9734b38d51555eb81bdadb7fd8965c21971.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$THTHH$\" width=\"76\" height=\"12\" />, which has a probability of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/a/efa6bbb2b2314d7bce95ec0bb3032a676bc74b7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2^5} = \\frac{1}{32}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"65\" height=\"37\" />. Furthermore, she can prolong her coin flipping by adding an extra <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/c/51ce23ae60cf4abdf055d93fa3d9fc5b7123b661.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TH$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />, which itself has a probability of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/c/45c4851bdd75eb0104d2ac1e7fd5eacf2d1065ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2^2} = \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"56\" height=\"37\" />. Since she can do this indefinitely, this gives an infinite geometric series with a first term of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/9/f99038cfb4c72100160971a30c90eaf4fd831001.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{32}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> and a common ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, which means the answer (by the infinite geometric series sum formula) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/4/224b66172ffb673956814af957582583c4406e2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{1}{32}}{1-\\frac{1}{4}} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{1}{24}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"138\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alternative_finish\">Alternative finish</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Alternative finish\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>You have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/348503b1f7c433de94e3b8f0d55037e4de77a08d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$THT$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />...(insert any # of pairs of HT)...HH. You could have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> pairs, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> pair, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> pairs, etc. of HT. Thus the probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/7/9c7cfcc15483cda7475922d883e8c91e32945c67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{1}{2})^0+(\\frac{1}{2})^2+(\\frac{1}{2})^4+...=\\frac{1}{(1-(\\frac{1}{2})^2)}=4/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"345\" height=\"45\" />. The number of ways to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e84fe5501ffa7630d72575bac33c9c313fb2dfbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$THT...HH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"14\" /> in that order is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5934160415e9730c72fdd596a8634dcdf19f24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8} * \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"45\" height=\"38\" />. Thus your probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/6/5461930c01b40113989df2b1082528041cd09668.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8} * \\frac{4}{3} * \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{1}{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"122\" height=\"38\" /> as desired\n</p><p>~mathboy282\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>~minor LaTeX edits by turttheturtlez\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Easier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Easier)\">Solution 2 (Easier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Easier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the sequence must start in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/348503b1f7c433de94e3b8f0d55037e4de77a08d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$THT$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, which happens with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db9e227e8177d26de452c2a2faeb6d45cc53d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> probability. Now, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the probability that Debra will get two heads in a row after flipping <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/348503b1f7c433de94e3b8f0d55037e4de77a08d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$THT$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. Either Debra flips two heads in a row immediately (probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />), or flips a head and then a tail and reverts back to the \"original position\" (probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/c/afc08682061d1c004e0508976f206da783704362.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"38\" />). Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/d/4dd4adbc0fb96c2d295a303af2b8247df9f18dc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{4}P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"101\" height=\"37\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/7/e4783ef2eec68a5ce7eb3fa53dcac57a2ef41e11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"50\" height=\"37\" />, so our final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/e/fbe01ff1b6be7c9dce21b6cc6af3cfff1f2e1aaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8}\\times\\frac{1}{3}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{1}{24}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"141\" height=\"48\" />.   \n</p><p>~Stormersyle\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Even_Easier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Even_Easier)\">Solution 3 (Even Easier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Even Easier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the sequence must start with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/348503b1f7c433de94e3b8f0d55037e4de77a08d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$THT$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> and end with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/0/85067484837402cff430e516ceaeb1406990d0cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> and only have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/6/9f67af52990263cfe29fddb11634154acda99653.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HT$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> in between, we use the infinite geometric series formula to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/f/19f100db6574f9961c8a708d8fe20ea1121e3835.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2^5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"19\" height=\"37\" /> which is the smallest option, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/4/534df9734b38d51555eb81bdadb7fd8965c21971.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$THTHH$\" width=\"76\" height=\"12\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/3/083e36f1d906cd751ff248cbf66856dbf090a959.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+\\frac{1}{2^7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"36\" height=\"38\" />, the next best option, and so on and so forth until we have an infinite geometric series increasing at a rate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/b/e6b2fd70f02e126584881ab1a990644af6cc057c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X\\frac{1}{2^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"39\" height=\"38\" /> so it is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/e/c1edc12257768a430c495b1a09a50fa6189ae744.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{1}{2^5}}{1-\\frac{1}{2^2}}=\\frac{1}{2^5}\\cdot\\frac{2^2}{3}=\\frac{1}{3\\cdot2^3}=\\frac{1}{8\\cdot3}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{1}{24}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"352\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>~&lt;B+\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/wopflrvUN2c?t=993\">https://youtu.be/wopflrvUN2c?t=993</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OnTheSpotSTEM\">Video Solution by OnTheSpotSTEM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OnTheSpotSTEM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2f1zEvfUe9o\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2f1zEvfUe9o</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B\">2019 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017171322\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.059 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 275/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6242/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.136      1 -total\n 60.51%    7.948      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 38.45%    5.051      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17285:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017171322 and revision id 289934. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}